    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659-a2">

                <pb facs="0602" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg526"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Sam Houston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1254. General Bell forwards the following from the Consul at Chihuahua: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#center">[Extract.]</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chihuahua</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April 15, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </p>
                        <p>Following is from General John J. Pershing</p>
                        <p>“Report Villa has gone southwest from San Borja.</p>
                        <p>No food, no forage of any description vicinity of Santa Cruz, where
                            troops now are. Shall withdraw them by easy marches in direction of
                            Satevo. Cannot supply them from San Antonio.</p>
                        <p>I am <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> to Namiquipa.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Funston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
